  "title": "rapid-hemifield-object-eeg",
  "description": "This EEG dataset investigates the neural dynamics of visual object coding across brain hemispheres. Object and word stimuli were rapidly presented (5Hz) in the left visual field, right visual field, or centrally, while participants engaged in an orthogonal red-target detection task. The dataset supports investigation of within- and cross-hemisphere object representation dynamics using frequency-tagging EEG paradigms.",
  "methods_description": "Object and word stimuli were presented at a rapid rate of 5Hz in the left or right visual field or centrally, while participants performed an orthogonal red target detection task, with EEG recorded throughout.",
